# The checks tests/test_channel.py runs on channel.cpp, and every finding fails it.
# Switched off, each for its reason - measured on 2 October 2026, none of them found a fault here:
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters    an address and a count are both numbers; style
#   bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion   sscanf with a %n that all_read checks, and
#                                           every argument comes from our own Python
#   performance-no-int-to-ptr               reading memory at a given address is the whole job
#   performance-enum-size                   four counters
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise                 new in clang-tidy 23; its 24 findings on 3 October 2026 were
#                                           Windows constants (PAGE_*, the lParam bits of a key), byte
#                                           masks on a promoted char, and pipe buffer sizes
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -performance-enum-size
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
